UPDATE companies SET description='Airlite Plastics Co. operates from Omaha, Nebraska, as a family-owned packaging manufacturer. The company emphasizes its long history while focusing on future-oriented innovation, though a specific founding year is not disclosed.

The company produces in-mold labeled (IML) and round containers, lids, and drink cups, including oxygen-barrier versions that incorporate an EVOH layer to extend shelf life. Its proprietary FDA-approved resin blends are used across product lines such as cultured foods, household items, horticulture containers, and high-pressure processing (HPP) applications. Engineering services, custom graphics, package design, and marketing support round out the offering.

Airlite serves brands in cultured dairy, household products, horticulture, and temperature-controlled shipping, providing packaging that withstands HPP and cold-chain requirements. Customers range from food processors needing oxygen-barrier containers to horticultural suppliers and consumer-goods companies seeking custom-decorated cups and lids.

