UPDATE companies SET description='Albuquerque Apparel Center operates in Albuquerque, New Mexico, as a statewide hub for the apparel and accessory industry. The organization does not disclose a founding year, ownership structure, or founder names in its public materials. It was established to connect designers, suppliers, production houses, and merchants across New Mexico, providing a physical and online infrastructure for the sector.

The center delivers a range of services rather than manufactured goods. It runs a networking hub that promotes New Mexico apparel through events, fashion shows, and multi-media advertising. A physical location allows designers to sell directly to retail customers while accessing wholesale buyers. The online platform NMFashionInfo.com serves as a directory for stores, supplies, services, and events statewide. The center also offers custom design and pattern services, operates the AAC School of Fashion Design with classes in flat pattern drafting, draping, and sewing, and provides mentorship programs. Community initiatives include fashion design classes for battered women''s groups and rehabilitation facilities.

Its audience spans the fashion and apparel industry: independent designers, start-up brands, production houses, suppliers, merchants, and students. The center also works with social-service organizations to deliver vocational training. Customers include New Mexico-based apparel companies and individuals seeking education, networking, or promotional support.

The organization states its mission is to foster growth of New Mexico''s apparel industry by connecting local companies, guiding start-ups, and providing education. It positions itself as a support system for talent that otherwise lacks infrastructure, aiming to make New Mexico a recognized fashion center leveraging the state''s lower cost of living and distinctive Southwest, Native American, and Western styles.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Networking and industry promotion", "Custom design and pattern services", "Fashion design education and workshops", "Mentorship programs for schools and organizations", "Community fashion design classes for social-service groups", "Online industry directory (NMFashionInfo.com)", "Retail sales venue for designers", "Wholesale buyer connection services"], "industries": ["Fashion & Apparel", "Apparel Accessories"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Industrial sewing machines", "Single-needle sewing machines", "Serger machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Statewide networking hub with multi-media promotion and fashion events", "Physical retail outlet for designers alongside wholesale buyer access", "Online industry directory NMFashionInfo.com covering stores, supplies, and events", "Custom design and pattern services for apparel start-ups", "Fashion design school offering classes in pattern drafting, draping, and sewing"], "facts_used": ["Location: Albuquerque, New Mexico -> db", "Operates as statewide hub for apparel industry -> /about", "Provides networking hub and promotion -> /about", "Offers physical retail outlet for designers -> /about", "Operates online directory NMFashionInfo.com -> /about", "Provides custom design and pattern services -> /about", "Runs AAC School of Fashion Design with classes in pattern drafting, draping, sewing -> /about", "Offers mentorship programs for schools and organizations -> /about", "Community involvement with battered women''s g