UPDATE companies SET description='Albuquerque Cabling, based in Albuquerque, New Mexico, has provided low-voltage infrastructure services since its founding in 1986. The company operates under the name ABQ Cabling and emphasizes a founding principle of completing every job correctly the first time.

The firm delivers ICT design and installation through a design-build model, holding a Registered Communications Distribution Designer (RCDD) on staff. Services span Category 6 and Category 6A network cabling, all low-voltage cable types, fiber-optic solutions, access-control systems, audio-visual installations, security and surveillance systems, and Valcom PA and paging systems. The company describes itself as the only New Mexico low-voltage contractor offering full design-build with custom ICT solutions.

Customers include government agencies, K-12 and higher-education institutions, and commercial businesses across New Mexico. Reference projects cite Exus Renewables North America, which relied on ABQ Cabling as a local partner for a new office build-out, and Albuquerque Academy, where the director of technology has engaged the firm on numerous projects over several years.

