UPDATE companies SET description='Alcan Electric & Engineering, Inc. was founded in 1971 in Anchorage, Alaska. The company is Alaskan-owned and operated, and has grown from a traditional electrical contractor into a full-service electrical, communications, security, and audio-visual technology integrator. It now employs over 200 professionals across offices in Anchorage, Fairbanks, Juneau, and Wasilla, serving the entire state.

The firm delivers commercial electrical construction services including power distribution, lighting, backup power, high-voltage, and design & engineering. It also integrates low-voltage systems such as building automation, IP video surveillance (as Alaska''s Milestone video pioneer), access control, structured cabling (BICSI-certified copper and fiber, and the state''s only Corning preferred installer), unified communications, and audio-visual solutions. Additional offerings include turn-key commercial solar, EV charging infrastructure, and electrical maintenance programs aligned with the 2023 NFPA 70B standard. With a workforce of more than 200 and three regional offices, Alcan handles large, complex projects across Alaska.

Alcan serves healthcare, aviation, corrections, defense, and North Slope industrial clients statewide. Notable projects include a 15-year partnership with Providence Alaska Medical Center in Anchorage encompassing the 82,000-square-foot Tower M, electrical work for the 16-bay F-35 hangars at Eielson Air Force Base, and advanced controls for the Anchorage Fish Hatchery. The company also works with commercial and energy-efficient lighting projects across the state.

The company emphasizes its Alaskan ownership and deep local knowledge of conditions, codes, and logistics as a key differentiator. It highlights the scale of its workforce and its NECA and IBEW Local 1547 affiliations, which provide trained, certified craftspeople and a deep labor pool. Alcan also promotes its integrated approach — combining electrical and low-voltage technology under one roof — and a formal safety program called "Safety Zone" that goes beyond compliance with weekly project-specific safety meetings.', certifications=ARRAY['BICSI','NFPA 70B']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Commercial electrical construction", "Power distribution", "Lighting design and installation", "Backup power systems", "High-voltage electrical work", "Electrical design and engineering", "Electrical system integration", "Building automation", "Security and access control systems", "IP video surveillance", "Access control", "Communications and VoIP", "Structured cabling (copper and fiber)", "Audio visual systems", "Commercial solar installation", "EV charging station installation", "NFPA 70B electrical maintenance", "Safety program management"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Aviation", "Corrections", "Defense", "North Slope industry", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Government"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Alaskan-owned and operated since 1971", "Over 200 professionals across three Alaska offices", "NECA and IBEW Local 1547 affiliated with certified craftspeople", "Integrated electrical and low-voltage technology under one roof", "Alaska''s only Corning preferred installer and Milestone video pioneer"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1971 -> db, /about", "200+ employees -> db, /, /about", "Alaskan-owned -> /, /about", "Offices in Anchorage, Fairbanks, Juneau, Wasilla -> /, /about", "Services: commercial electrical, system integration, security, communications, structured cabling, audio visual, solar, EV charging, NFPA 70B maintenance -> /services", "Industries: healthcare, aviation, corrections, defense, North Slope -> /, /about", "Projects: Providence Alaska Medical Center Tower M, Eielson AFB F-35 hangars, Anchorage Fish Hatchery -> /", "BICSI-certified copper & fiber -> /, /services", "Corning preferred installer -> /, /services", "Milestone video pioneer -> /, /services", "NECA & IBEW Local 1547 affiliations -> /about", "Safety Zone program -> /about", "NFPA 70B maintenance aligned to 2023 standard -> /services", "Commercial solar turn-key -> /services", "EV charging stations Level 2 and DC fast -> /services", "Integrated partner for electrical and low-voltage -> /, /about", "Built for Alaska conditions, codes, logistics -> /", "Scale to staff large complex builds -> /", "Trained certified craftspeople -> /about", "One integrated partner -> /", "Alaska''s only Corning preferred installer -> /", "Alaska''s Milestone video pioneer -> /", "BICSI-certified -> /", "NFPA 70B -> /services"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Alcan Electrical & Engineering is one of Alaska''s largest electrical contractors, owned and operated by Alaskans.", "founded_year": "1971", "employee_count": "200+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='alcan-electric-engineering-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Alconex Magnet Wire operates from Fort Wayne, Indiana, where it manufactures custom magnet wire and extrusion products for a global market. The American-owned company specializes in continuous extrusion and wire wrapping of aluminum and copper alloys, producing bare and insulated wire in round, square, and rectangular profiles.

The company''s capabilities cover the full range from single reels to multiple truckloads, with packaging options that include continuous spools, reel-less coils, and straight lengths. Its Fort Wayne facility extrudes custom aluminum shapes and supplies magnet wire used in electric vehicles, traction motors, alternators, electric motors, lifting magnets, and welders, as well as mechanical applications that do not require electrification.

Alconex serves industries ranging from automotive electrification and industrial power equipment to general mechanical fabrication. Customers include manufacturers of electric vehicle drivetrains, industrial lifting magnets, welding equipment, and a variety of motor and alternator builders who rely on the company''s quick-turn made-to-order lead times.

