UPDATE companies SET description='Alert Tech SMT is an electronics contract manufacturer based in Webster, Texas. The company began as a retail technology business before pivoting to full‑stack contract manufacturing to meet demand for scalable, customized PCB assembly runs.

The company provides full‑service surface‑mount technology (SMT) assembly and turnkey printed circuit board assembly, including component sourcing, PCB fabrication, cable harness and box‑build integration, new‑product introduction (NPI) and prototyping, and a range of in‑house testing (functional, flying‑probe, RF, optical inspection) and repair services. Production spans prototype through volume runs, supported by equipment such as a TAKAYA flying‑probe tester, 3D printers and CO₂ lasers.

Alert Tech serves customers in telecommunications, industrial technology, robotics and drones, military and defense, energy, aerospace, and medical devices. Testimonials cite clients in industrial technology and oil and gas, and the company notes work with federal agencies and firms in aerospace and energy.

The firm was created to address the difficulty of obtaining scalable, customized electronics runs by bringing production in‑house and offering a single‑point‑of‑contact model. It emphasizes a service‑driven approach with proactive communication, a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015, and a goal of zero item failures.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','IPC-A-610 Class 3']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["SMT component sourcing and procurement", "PCB fabrication management", "Turnkey SMT assembly", "Cable harness and point-to-point wiring", "Sub-assembly", "Enclosure modification and assembly", "Final unit test (FUT)", "Box build and system integration", "Burn-in testing", "Configure and build to order", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Prototype and volume production", "New product introduction (NPI)", "Design review", "BOM and configuration control support", "Stencil design", "Integrated process development", "Full-service documentation", "Functional testing", "Flying probe testing (TAKAYA)", "Board and system-level testing", "RF performance testing", "Custom test fixture and software implementation", "Optical inspection", "Compliance testing and support", "Field service return and repair", "End-of-life (EOL)/obsolescence management", "Failure mode and effects analysis (FMEA)", "Custom board refurbishing", "3D printing for fixtures and enclosures", "CO\u2082 laser cutting/engraving"], "industries": ["Telecommunications", "Industrial Technology", "Robotics", "Drones", "Military", "Defense", "Energy", "Aerospace", "Medical Devices", "Oil and Gas", "Federal Government"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["TAKAYA Flying Probe Tester", "3D printers", "CO\u2082 lasers"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single point of contact for sourcing, development, fabrication and delivery", "In-house testing including flying-probe, functional, RF and optical inspection", "Turnkey box\u2011build and system integration under o