UPDATE companies SET description='All Energy Solar was founded in 2009 by brothers Michael and Brian Allen in Westfield, Massachusetts. The company began as a solar installation provider focused on helping property owners transition to clean energy.

The firm delivers turnkey solar solutions for residential, commercial, and utility-scale projects. Its service scope covers site assessment, custom system design, permitting, installation, and lifetime monitoring. For larger developments, the team handles feasibility analysis, grid interconnection, and solar farm construction.

Customers include homeowners, businesses such as office buildings, warehouses, manufacturing facilities, retail spaces, agricultural operations, and nonprofits, as well as municipalities and energy developers seeking utility-scale installations. The company operates primarily across Massachusetts, navigating state-specific incentives like the SMART program and net metering.

All Energy Solar distinguishes itself through a staff that includes NABCEP-certified professionals and fully licensed contractors, emphasizing custom-designed systems rather than one-size-fits-all approaches. The founders started the business to provide a seamless, locally informed path to solar adoption, managing every detail from consultation to long-term support.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar installation (residential, commercial, utility-scale)", "Site assessment", "Custom system design", "Permitting", "Lifetime monitoring", "Feasibility analysis", "Grid interconnection", "Solar farm development", "Solar incentive consulting", "Net metering application assistance", "SMART program enrollment", "Tax credit processing"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Utility-scale solar", "Agricultural", "Nonprofit", "Municipal", "Energy development", "Manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["NABCEP-certified professionals on staff", "Fully licensed contractors for all installations", "Custom-designed systems tailored to each property", "Turnkey service from site assessment to lifetime monitoring", "Deep expertise in Massachusetts solar incentives (SMART, net metering, tax credits)"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2009 by brothers Michael and Brian Allen -> db", "Headquartered in Westfield, Massachusetts -> db", "Provides residential, commercial, and utility-scale solar installation -> /", "Offers turnkey services including site assessment, design, permitting, installation, monitoring -> /", "Serves homeowners, businesses, municipalities, developers -> /", "Employs NABCEP-certified professionals and licensed contractors -> /", "Custom-designed solutions for each property -> /", "Expertise in Massachusetts incentives (SMART program, net metering, tax credits) -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "All Energy Solar offers expert solar installation in Massachusetts for homes and businesses.", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='all-energy-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='All Original Foods, Inc. is a specialty and Italian food distributor based in Bessemer, Alabama. The company was founded in 1964 by Dewaine Carlson, who aimed to bring authentic pizza products to the South. He partnered with a New York-based company to establish the Original Crispy Pizza Crust Company of Alabama. Today, the business remains under second-generation family ownership and management.

The company distributes an extensive line of Italian and specialty food products sourced globally. It operates a test kitchen where products are tested, compared, and tasted before being offered to customers. All Original Foods also provides education and hands-on training to its clients. As a member of Bellissimo Foods, a nationwide association of Italian food distributors, it leverages collective buying power to access a broad selection of ingredients.

