UPDATE companies SET description='Allied Body Works Inc. was founded in 1949 in Seattle, Washington, when Charles Walter Bull and two partners each invested $200 to leave Heiser Body and open a small garage on Fourth Avenue. The business has remained family-owned through four generations, passing from Bull to his son Owen and son-in-law Dick Minice, then to Richard Minice in 1996, and most recently to great-grandson Adam Keane, who purchased the company in February 2023 and serves as president.

The company operates as a full-line truck equipment distributor and upfitter, providing custom fabrication, installation, and repair for light- to medium-duty vehicles. Its shop builds service bodies, dump bodies, platform bodies, flatbeds, contractor bodies, and van bodies, and integrates cranes, liftgates, electrical and lighting accessories, and EV power systems. Allied also offers cargo van interiors, truck side guards (marketed as the Walker Blocker), and a ready-now inventory program through a partnership with Work Truck Solutions.

A dedicated government and fleet account team handles public-sector contracts.

The company emphasizes its family-owned culture as a differentiator, citing a standard of excellence that carries into every build. It highlights quick turnaround to meet deadlines, the ability to execute complex custom plans, and a future-focused mindset that includes safety innovations like the Walker Blocker and green options such as solar integration. The stated mission is to listen to each customer and design a solution that fits their specific operational needs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Van Upfitting", "Truck Upfitting", "Fabrication", "Repair", "EV Solutions", "Truck Side Guards (Walker Blocker)", "Cargo Van Interiors", "Service Bodies", "Dump Bodies", "Platform Bodies", "Flatbeds", "Contractor Bodies", "Van Bodies", "Crane Installation", "Electrical and Lighting Accessories", "Liftgate Installation", "Parts Sales", "Ready-Now Inventory (via Work Truck Solutions)"], "industries": ["Tradespeople", "Fleet Management", "Government", "Construction", "Shipping and Distribution", "Utilities", "Armored Transport", "Commercial Fleets", "Mobile Workforce"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Walker Blocker", "E-Power Systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned operation with a multi-generational commitment to customers and employees", "Quick installation turnaround with deadlines as top priority", "Experienced technicians capable of executing complex custom plans", "Future-focused innovations including the Walker Blocker side-guard system and solar integration", "Customer-centric design process that listens and tailors each solution"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1949 by Charles Walter Bull and two partners with $200 each -> /about", "Family-owned through four generations, current owner Adam Keane (great-grandson) purchased Feb 2023 -> /about", "Headquarters at 625 South 96th Street, Seattle, WA 98108 -> /", "Full-line truck equipment distributor and upfitter offering custom fabrication, installa