UPDATE companies SET description='American Cable & Electronics, Inc. operates from Menomonee Falls, Wisconsin, where it manufactures custom cable assemblies and electro-mechanical assemblies for original equipment manufacturers.

The company specializes in engineering, rapid prototyping, and low-volume production of complex electromechanical assemblies. Its capabilities span simple wire harnesses to finished assemblies that integrate plastics, sheet metal, electronics, cable assemblies, and plastic-injected overmolded parts. Services include low-volume overmolding with flexible tooling, custom cable assemblies, D-sub and BNC connector assemblies, high-definition video and data-center cables, embedded circuits, overmolded PCBs, and turnkey electro-mechanical projects.

Its customer base includes OEMs in medical electronics, industrial controls, and commercial products, as well as the U.S. and Canadian departments of defense. The firm is a Tier 1 supplier to the medical industry and holds registrations for defense work.

ACE differentiates itself through a focus on low-volume manufacturing excellence, emphasizing attention to detail, communication across staff and suppliers, and process controls designed to ensure first-time quality. Engineering support covers design for manufacturability, design assistance, material analysis and testing, tooling development, and CAD services, backed by a global procurement strategy aimed at on-time delivery.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','IPC/WHMA-A-620','UL/CSA','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Low volume overmolding with flexible tooling", "Custom cable assemblies", "D-sub cable assemblies (all pin configurations)", "BNC/RF connector assemblies for coaxial cable", "High definition video cable assemblies", "Data center cables", "Embedded circuits or overmolded PCB", "Turn-key electro-mechanical projects", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Design assistance", "Material analysis and testing", "Tooling development", "CAD services", "Rapid prototyping", "Electromechanical assembly (plastics, sheet metal, electronics, cable assemblies, overmolded parts)", "Wire harness assemblies"], "industries": ["Medical electronics", "Defense (U.S. and Canadian Departments of Defense)", "Industrial controls", "Commercial products"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Low to mid volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Low-volume manufacturing expertise with focus on first-time quality", "Engineering services including DFM, design assistance, material analysis, tooling development, CAD", "Global procurement strategy for on-time material availability", "Attention to detail and communication across staff and suppliers", "Process controls ensuring every product manufactured correctly the first time"], "facts_used": ["Company name and description -> db", "Headquarters: Menomonee Falls, Wisconsin -> db", "Certifications: ISO 9001, RoHS -> db", "Products: Custom cables and cable assemblies for OEM market -> db", "Industries served: Medical, Defense, Industrial controls, Commercial -> db", "Specializes in engineering, rapid prototype, low volume electromechanical assemblies -> /", "Capabilities: low volume overmolding, custom cable assemblies, D-sub, BNC, HD video, data center cables, embedded circuits, overmolded PCB, turnkey electro-mechanical -> /capabilities", "Clients: top OEMs in medical electronics, industrial controls, commercial products -> /about-us", "Tier 1 medical industry supplier -> /about-us", "JCP USA/Canadian Departments of Defense -> /", "ISO 9001 Registered, IPC/WHMA-A-620, UL/CSA, RoHS compliant -> /", "Engineering services: DFM, design assistance, material analysis/testing, tooling development, CAD -> /about-us", "Global materials procurement strategy -> /about-us", "Focus on low volume manufacturing excellence, attention to detail, communication, process controls -> /", "Differentiators: understanding customer needs, industry leaders in engineering and production -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Manufacturer of Custom Cables and Cable Assemblies for the OEM Market", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='american-cable-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='American Cable Products, LLC was established in November 2002 in Lake St Louis, Missouri. The minority-owned business (MBE certified) began as a provider of low‑voltage communication connectivity solutions, aiming to serve organizations across the United States, Canada, Mexico, and U.S. territories.

The company delivers end‑to‑end infrastructure services divided into inside‑plant and outside‑plant work. Inside‑plant capabilities include structured premise cabling (Cat5e, Cat6, Cat6a, and fiber), data‑center design and implementation, hardware configuration, and network infrastructure. Outside‑plant services cover provider connection points, fiber‑optic installations, campus connectivity, and inter‑building links. A security and surveillance division installs IP camera systems, access‑control and biometric solutions, with project experience exceeding 2,800 cameras. The firm also provides wireless networks, VoIP, audio‑visual, SCADA/industrial IoT, satellite communications, consulting, and ongoing maintenance. Operations span all 50 states, with regional offices supporting a project portfolio that includes 500‑plus facilities and 1,000‑plus sites.

Clients range from Fortune 500 enterprises to critical‑infrastructure operators in sectors such as data centers, healthcare, corrections, education, airports, government, retail, and manufacturing. Named references include St. Louis Lambert International Airport, a multi‑site healthcare network, a university system, a retail distribution chain, and an industrial manufacturing complex.

American Cable Products states its mission is to be a one‑stop shop for communication connectivity from the provider demarcation point to the client data center, delivering practical, high‑quality, and cost‑effective IT installation and service while exceeding customer expectations. Core values cited are quality, reliability, customer focus, and cost effectiveness.', certifications=ARRAY['MBE Certified (Minority Business Enterprise)','CPUC Certified (California Public Utilities Commission)','St. Louis Lambert International Airport approved contractor']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Inside plant services (structured premise cabling, data center implementation, hardware configuration, network infrastructure)", "Outside plant services (provider connection points, fiber optic installations, campus connectivity, inter-building connections)", "Security & surveillance (camera & video systems, access control & biometrics, system integration)", "Structured cabling (Cat5e, Cat6, Cat6a, fiber optic)", "Data center design, build, and implementation", "Hardware setup and configuration", "System integration (enterprise-wide communication systems)", "Wireless solutions (enterprise-grade wireless networks)", "Video surveillance (IP cameras and monitoring systems)", "Voice systems (VoIP and traditional phone systems)", "Audio visual (conference and collaboration systems)", "SCADA & industrial (industrial control and IoT connectivity)", "Satellite communications (remote and backup connectivity)", "Consulting (infrastructure strategy guidance)", "Maintenance (ongoing support and service)"], "industries": ["Data Centers", "Healthcare", "Corrections", "Education", "Airports", "Government", "Retail", "Manufacturing"], "materials": ["Cat5e", "Cat6", "Cat6a", "Fiber optic"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["MBE Certified (Minority Business Enterprise)", "CPUC Certified (California Public Utilities Commission for telecommunications infra