UPDATE companies SET description='American Circuits operates from Charlotte, North Carolina, where it has maintained a family-run, minority-owned contract manufacturing business for over 30 years. The company was founded by Vic Gondha, a first-generation immigrant who built the firm after arriving in the United States with a goal of owning a business. His son, Ket Gondha, now serves as CEO, having expanded the campus to two facilities totaling roughly 40,000 square feet.

The company provides turnkey printed circuit board assembly from bare-board fabrication through final box-build integration. Its services span SMT, through-hole, and mixed-technology assembly, rapid prototyping, conformal coating and potting, automated optical inspection, PCB design and reverse engineering, design-for-manufacturability analysis, BOM optimization, custom wire-harness and cable assembly, and full electro-mechanical integration. Production runs range from single prototypes to volumes exceeding 100,000 units.

American Circuits serves approximately 400 customers across defense, healthcare, robotics, and LED-lighting sectors. Named clients include TE Connectivity, Honda, and Assa Abloy, the latter a Charlotte-based security and access-control manufacturer.

The firm distinguishes itself by controlling the entire process from bare-board supply to finished assembly, a combination it says few competitors offer. It emphasizes U.S.-based manufacturing, engineering support at every stage, flexible production runs, and rapid turnarounds. The operation is ISO 9001 certified, ITAR registered, UL recognized, and compliant with RoHS, REACH, and Dodd-Frank conflict-mineral requirements.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ITAR','UL recognized','RoHS','REACH','Dodd-Frank conflict mineral reporting']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB fabrication", "PCB assembly (SMT, through-hole, mixed technology)", "Turnkey production", "Rapid prototyping", "Conformal coating", "Potting", "Automated optical inspection (AOI)", "PCB design", "Reverse engineering", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "BOM optimization", "Wire harness assembly", "Cable assembly", "Electro-mechanical assembly", "Box build integration", "Custom enclosures and fixtures", "Assembly-to-order (ATO)", "Kitting", "Testing"], "industries": ["Defense", "Healthcare", "Robotics", "LED lighting"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "1 to 100,000+ units", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Controls entire process from bare-board fabrication to finished assembly", "Turnkey assembly for prototype quantities from 1 to 100,000+ units", "U.S.-based manufacturing with engineering support at every stage", "ISO 9001 certified, ITAR registered, UL recognized", "Family-owned, minority-owned business with over 30 years'' history"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Charlotte, North Carolina -> db", "Founded by Vic Gondha, first-generation immigrant -> /about-us", "Family-run, minority-owned -> /about-us", "Over 30 years history -> /about-us", "Two facilities totaling roughly 40,000 sq ft -> /, /about-us", "Services: PCB manufacturing & assembly, turnkey, prototyping, conformal coating, AOI, design, reverse engineering, DFM, BOM optimization, wire harness, electro-mechanical assembly -> /", "Certifications: ISO 9001, ITAR, UL recognized, RoHS, REACH, Dodd-Frank -> /, /quality", "Customers: TE Connectivity, Honda, Assa Abloy; approx 400 customers -> /about-us", "Industries: defense, healthcare, robotics, LED lighting -> /about-us", "Volume range: 1 to 100,000+ units -> /about-us", "Ribbon-cutting October 2024 for new 37,000 sq ft facilities -> /about-us", "CEO Ket Gondha, Max Johnson operations -> /about-us", "Environmental Excellence Platinum Award 5 straight years -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "American Circuits is an electronic contract manufacturer specializing in turnkey PCB services from design to box builds.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "1 unit", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Minority-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='american-circuits' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='American Control Electronics (ACE) operates from South Beloit, Illinois, with a second facility in Chanhassen, Minnesota. The company is part of the Global Point Technologies Group and traces its roots back more than six decades in motor control design and manufacturing, though a specific founding year is not publicly stated.

ACE manufactures electronic motor controls, power products, and custom electronic assemblies. Its capabilities span custom circuit design, PCB layout and assembly, electronic contract manufacturing, UL508A control panel assembly, wire harness and box build, as well as testing and compliance support. The Chanhassen site runs an ISO 9001:2015-certified quality system, while the South Beloit plant handles UL508A panel assembly and in-house UL testing via the UL Data Acceptance Program.

The company serves OEMs across industrial, food processing, medical, automotive, agriculture, scientific, oil and gas, and sports markets, among others. It also supports home automation and commercial facility systems through its motor control product lines.

ACE emphasizes its 60-plus years of experience and its integration within the Global Point Technologies network, which provides manufacturing intelligence across the Americas and Asia. The firm also highlights flexible circuit technologies through its GOT Interface brand, enabling lightweight, adaptable interfaces for medical, industrial, and IoT applications.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','UL Listed','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom circuit design", "PCB design", "PCB assembly (PCBA)", "Electronic contract manufacturing (EMS)", "Engineering design process", "Testing, compliance & support", "UL508A control panel assembly", "Wire harness assembly", "Box build", "Flexible circuit technologies (polyester, polyimide, transparent touch sensors, fabric circuits)", "Multi-sensor integration (medical, industrial, flexible force, non-invasive fluid level)", "Wired and wireless interconnectivity solutions", "Digital graphics (dead-fronted graphics, offset/screen/digital printing, thermoformed designs)", "Touch screen interface (capacitive touch, infrared sensing, membrane switches, 3D gesturing)", "IoT device design and manufacturing", "Embedded display controllers", "Switch actuators (tactile, non-tactile, 3D gesturing)", "Enclosures for electronics (mechatronics, in-mold decorating, in-mold electronics)", "Motor control design and manufacturing (DC, AC, brushless, stepper, servo)", "Gear reducers", "Legacy product support", "Cross reference services", "Product selection tools"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Food Processing", "Service", "Medical", "Home", "Automotive", "Agriculture", "Scientific", "Oil & Gas", "Sports"], "materials": ["Polyester", "Polyimide", "Transparent materials", "Fabric"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["60+ years of experience in motor control design and manufacturing", "Dual U.S. facilities in South Beloit, IL and Chanhassen, MN with ISO 9001:2015 certification at Chanhassen