UPDATE companies SET description='American Iron Works operates from a shop in New Haven, Connecticut. The business traces its roots back over 40 years to a passion for metal craft held by Pasquale, the father and grandfather of the current owners. Today it is a third‑generation, family‑owned company led by Anthony and Joe Maresca, who have grown the operation into a full‑service fabrication and installation house serving clients across Connecticut.

The company produces custom ornamental metal fabrications in iron, stainless steel, aluminum, and bronze. Its in‑house capabilities span welding (Stick, MIG, TIG), metal forming (grinding, cutting, chamfering, bending, punching, shearing, and CNC plasma cutting), and finishing (sandblasting, powder coating, galvanizing, and patinas). Every project moves through material sourcing, fabrication, finishing, and installation under one roof, with each piece inspected before it leaves the shop.

American Iron Works serves both commercial and residential customers. Commercial projects have included fire‑escape renovations, steel mezzanines, anti‑climb fencing, and custom partition walls for office and retail spaces. Residential work ranges from hand‑forged stair rails and Juliet balconies to aluminum pergolas, cable‑rail systems, and decorative gates. The shop also fabricates specialty items such as sunburst panels, branch‑textured railings, and custom signage.

The Maresca brothers emphasize fine craftsmanship, custom design, and efficiency as the pillars of their reputation. They attribute their longevity to a hands‑on approach that controls every step from raw material to final installation, ensuring each client receives a unique, detail‑oriented piece.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom ornamental metal fabrication", "Commercial iron services", "Residential iron services", "Welding (Stick, MIG, TIG)", "Metal grinding, cutting, chamfering, bending, punching, shearing", "CNC plasma cutting", "Sandblasting", "Powder coating", "Galvanizing", "Patina finishing", "Installation"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Residential construction", "Architectural metalwork"], "materials": ["Iron", "Stainless Steel", "Aluminum", "Bronze", "Steel"], "equipment": ["CNC plasma cutter", "Welding machines (Stick, MIG, TIG)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full in-house fabrication, finishing, and installation", "Third-generation family ownership", "Custom ornamental metalwork in iron, stainless steel, aluminum, and bronze", "Detail-oriented inspection on every piece", "Over 40 years of metal craft experience"], "facts_used": ["Location: 17 Morris, New Haven, CT 06519 -> /", "Family-owned, third-generation, founded by Pasquale, now Anthony & Joe Maresca -> /about", "Over 40 years of experience -> /", "Services: custom ornamental metal fabrication, commercial/residential iron services -> /", "Processes: welding (Stick, MIG, TIG), metal craft (grinding, cutting, chamfering, bending, punching, shearing, plasma cutting), finishing (sandblasting, powder coating, galvanizing, patinas) -> /", "Materials: Iron, Stainless Steel, Aluminum, Bronze -> /", "Equipment: CNC plasma cutter, welding equipment -> /", "Industries: commercial and residential customers across Connecticut -> /about", "Social media: @americanironworksllc -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "At American Iron Works, we offer custom made-to-order metal fabrications in Iron, Stainless Steel, Aluminum, Bronze and more.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://instagram.com/americanironworksllc"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='american-iron-works' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='American Metal Fabricators was founded in 1988 in Gastonia, North Carolina, just outside Charlotte. The company operates as a custom metal fabrication shop and has served the region for over three decades.

The company fabricates a wide range of custom equipment including air washers, air handling units, foam panels, energy recovery systems, dryers, ovens, furnaces, plenums, duct systems, dust filtration equipment, gas turbine filtration, mining equipment, humidification systems, mist eliminators, acoustic enclosures, scrubbers, spray systems, and evaporative cooling systems. It operates from a 200,000-square-foot manufacturing facility with a dedicated 30,000-square-foot sandblast building, high-bay overhead cranes, and drive-through truck access. The workforce includes welders, fabricators, pipefitters, electricians, machinists, painters, mechanics, designers, drafters, schedulers, expediters, QA/QC inspectors, and sales staff. Equipment includes 15 press brakes (up to 14 feet, 400+ tons), five shears (1/2-inch capacity, 12 feet), four plasma cutting tables (10 feet wide by 40 feet long), laser cutters, a 500-foot rail paint line with downdraft booth, foam panel injection equipment, and rolling capabilities for angle ring, pipe, and channel.

American Metal Fabricators serves industries such as power generation, utilities, microelectronics, paper, pulp, fibers, textiles, wood, furniture, food and beverage, chemicals, plastics, paint, printing, heavy equipment, and pharmaceuticals.

The company emphasizes its ability to handle complex jobs with short lead times, supported by a large skilled labor force that allows rapid expansion. It is equipped for both large-scale projects and special handling of smaller orders, with in-house capabilities spanning welding, forming, blasting, painting, rolling, assembly, and foam panel manufacturing.', certifications=ARRAY['ASTM E84','SNAP 2021']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom metal fabrication", "MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Stick welding", "Fluxcore welding", "Shearing (up to 1/2 in thick, 12 ft length)", "Press brake forming (up to 14 ft, 400+ tons)", "Plasma cutting (up to 10 ft wide \u00d7 40 ft long)", "Laser cutting", "Sandblasting (SP6\u2013SP10, media recovery)", "Painting (rail line, downdraft booth, chemical cleaning)", "Angle ring rolling", "Pipe rolling", "Channel rolling", "Large unit assembly", "Equipment staging", "Insulated foam panel manufacturing (injected polyurethane core)", "Foam panel door fabrication", "Duct door fabrication", "Marine access door fabrication", "Standard access door fabrication", "Pipe threading", "Design and drafting", "QA/QC inspection"], "industries": ["Power Generation", "Utilities", "Microelectronics", "Paper", "Pulp", "Fibers", "Textiles", "Wood", "Furniture", "Food & Beverage", "Chemicals", "Plastics & Paint", "Printing", "Heavy Equipment", "Pharmaceutical"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Carbon steel", "Embossed aluminum", "Galvanized steel", "OSB", "Polyurethane foam"], "equipment": ["15 press brakes (14 ft, 400+ tons)", "5 shears (1/2 in, 12 ft)", "4 plasma cutting tables (10 ft \u00d7 40 ft)", "Laser cutters", "Sandblast building (SP6\u2013SP10, media recovery)", "500 ft rail paint line with downdraft paint booth", "Foam panel injection equipment", "Overhead cranes", "Hoists", "Forklifts", "Pipe threading equipment", "MIG/TIG/Stick/Fluxcore welding machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [