UPDATE companies SET description='American Wire Group (AWG) is headquartered in Aventura, Florida, with operation centers in Perris, California; Mechanicsburg, Pennsylvania; and Katy, Texas. The company marks 25 years in business, having grown into a national supplier of wire, cable, hardware, and equipment for utility and renewable energy markets.

AWG manufactures and supplies a range of wire and cable products including aluminum, copper, steel, and fiber‑optic cables, as well as poles, pole‑line hardware, and accessories. Its value‑added services cover cable management and logistics, custom engineering and design, supply‑chain optimization, and emergency response. The company operates coast‑to‑coast warehouses and offers customization such as cut‑to‑length, paralleling, and custom labeling, along with reel disposal and specialty cable constructions.

The company serves utilities, renewable‑energy developers (wind, solar, battery energy storage), data‑center operators, EV and hydrogen‑fueling infrastructure projects, power transmission and distribution networks, substations, and industrial facilities. Government agencies and emergency‑response teams also rely on AWG for rapid material deployment during disaster recovery.

AWG emphasizes its extensive inventory and nationwide warehouse network as key differentiators, enabling delivery in days rather than weeks. Its ISO 9001:2015‑certified quality system and 24/7 emergency response capability are positioned as core reasons customers choose the company for mission‑critical projects.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire and cable manufacturing and supply", "Cable management and logistics", "Cable engineering and design", "Supply chain optimization", "Emergency response services", "Custom labeling", "Cut-to-length services", "Paralleling services", "Connectors and hardware supply", "Reel disposal and recycling", "Specialty cable constructions", "Material selection", "Bulk purchasing and customization", "Traceability and recycling", "Custom cable solutions", "Procurement and inventory management", "Warehousing and logistics (JIT delivery)", "Cost-effective sourcing and distribution", "Value-added services (customization, specialized solutions)", "Pole and pole-line hardware supply", "Transmission and distribution cable supply", "Medium voltage cable supply", "Low voltage cable supply", "Fiber optic cable supply"], "industries": ["Utility", "Renewable Energy", "Wind Power", "Solar Power", "Battery Energy Storage", "Data Centers", "EV Infrastructure", "Hydrogen-Powered Vehicle Infrastructure", "Power Transmission and Distribution", "Substations", "Industrial", "Government Agencies", "Emergency Response Teams"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Copper", "Steel", "Fiber Optic"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Delivery in days, not weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest and most extensive inventory of wire and cable products in the United States", "Coast-to-coast warehouse network enabling delivery in days, not weeks", "24/7 emergency response services for disaster recovery", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system", "Custom cable engineering and design services"], "facts_