UPDATE companies SET description='Americor Electronics Ltd. was founded in 1988 in Elk Grove Village, Illinois, by Tom Pross, who brought 22 years of experience in power cord, cable, and wire harness production.

The company manufactures custom and standard power cords, cable assemblies, and wire harnesses, along with a range of electronic components including solenoids, relays, axial fans, terminal blocks, piezoelectric devices, EMI/RFI filters, transformers, and adapters. It provides prototyping, testing, documentation for approval, and post‑order inventory management and shipping. Americor also serves as the U.S. manufacturer’s representative for Germany’s Adels Contact, supplying terminal blocks, connector systems, and distribution boxes for high‑power LEDs.

Americor sells exclusively to original equipment manufacturers and distributors, serving the appliance, electronics, and medical device sectors. Longtime customers include Pulsafeeder, an Idex Corporation business, which named Americor its Supplier of the Year in 2019. The company has supported OEM product development for over three decades.

Pross started the business to offer custom‑engineered products that guarantee maximum function and cost efficiency, backed by a commitment to stay current with certifications such as ISO 9001:2015 and RoHS compliance. The firm emphasizes ongoing service, managing inventory and logistics for clients after the initial order.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable assembly", "Wire harness manufacturing", "Prototyping and testing", "Documentation for submittal and approval", "Inventory management and shipping", "Power cord manufacturing", "Electronic component assembly (solenoids, relays, fans, connectors, piezoelectric devices)", "EMI/RFI line filter manufacturing", "Transformer manufacturing", "Adapter manufacturing", "Terminal block and connector system distribution (Adels Contact)"], "industries": ["OEM", "Appliance manufacturing", "Electronics manufacturing", "Medical device manufacturing", "Electrical equipment manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 certified and RoHS compliant", "Custom products designed to specifications with prototyping and testing support", "Post\u2011order inventory management and shipping services", "U.S. representative for Adels Contact (Germany) terminal blocks and connector systems", "Pulsafeeder Supplier of the Year award (2019)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1988 in Elk Grove Village, IL by Tom Pross -> /about", "Tom Pross had 22 years experience before founding -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certified and RoHS compliant -> /", "Manufactures power cords, cable & wire harnesses, electronic components -> /", "Provides prototyping, testing, documentation, inventory management -> /about", "U.S. manufacturer''s representative for Adels Contact (Germany) -> /", "Sells only to OEMs and distributors -> /", "Serves appliance, electronics, medical device industries -> /about, /", "Pulsafeeder Supplier of the Year 2019 -> /", "Wiring Harness Manufacturer''s Association Member -> /", "Headquarters: 675 S. Lively Blvd, Elk Grove Village, IL 60007 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Manufacturing power cords, cable & wire harnesses and other electric and electronic components for the world since 1988.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='americor-electronics-ltd' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ameriprint Apparel is a custom screen-printing and embroidery company based in Sun Prairie, Wisconsin. Founded in 1985, the business has served the local community and broader Wisconsin area for nearly four decades.

The company provides a range of decoration and customization services including screen printing, embroidery, direct-to-film (DTF) and digital printing, and laser engraving. It also sources and brands promotional products such as drinkware, headwear, tote bags, and office items. All production is handled in-house at its Sun Prairie facility, which includes a graphics team and an online design tool for customers.

Ameriprint serves schools, sports teams, corporate businesses, and organizations needing branded merchandise. Its customer base includes educational institutions ordering team and spirit wear, companies seeking employee appreciation kits and trade show giveaways, and groups such as the American Legion and university fraternities. The shop also handles holiday corporate gifts and promotional items for events.

