UPDATE companies SET description='Amphenol DC Electronics operates from a 70,000-square-foot facility in San Jose, California, with additional manufacturing sites in Nogales, Mexico, and Malaysia. The company was founded in 1979 by David Cianciulli after he left Hughes Aircraft to start a cable sales and distribution business. Within a few years, the operation added engineers and assemblers to produce custom cable and wire harness solutions for technical instrument manufacturers. In 2013, the business was acquired by Amphenol Corporation, becoming a division known as Amphenol DC Electronics (ADCE).

ADCE specializes in the design, engineering, and manufacture of custom wire harnesses, cable assemblies, and integrated electronic mechanical devices (box builds). The company handles both high- and low-volume production runs, offering build-to-print services, prototyping, and custom tooling design.

The company serves aerospace and military customers (notably supplying Trimble with GPS cables during the first Gulf War), medical device manufacturers (MRI, patient monitoring, surgical robotics), industrial equipment makers (factory automation robots), precision agriculture (GPS and surveying equipment), and RF coaxial applications. Its client base includes defense contractors, medical OEMs, and industrial automation firms.

ADCE emphasizes its single-focus expertise in custom cable and wire harness assemblies, which the company says enables engineers to identify design flaws before production. It highlights lean manufacturing practices applied across information and material flows, in-house engineering liaison services, and a culture of continuous improvement as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','ISO 13485:2003','ITAR','IPC-620:2016 Class III','UL 508','UL 764','C-TPAT','SAM','GDEP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable harnesses & assemblies", "Integrated electrical mechanical devices (box builds)", "Overmolded cable assemblies", "Discrete assemblies", "Medical device cables", "Value-added engineering and design liaison", "Lean manufacturing implementation", "CNC machining", "Press operations (30/55/85 ton)", "Clean room assembly (Class 1000, Class 10,000)", "Build-to-print manufacturing", "Prototyping and custom tooling design", "Smart cable assembly", "Semi-rigid coax cable fabrication", "Sub-miniature coax cabling", "Cable braiding", "Ruggedized assemblies", "Fiber optic cable assemblies", "UL 508 / UL 764 certified assemblies"], "industries": ["Medical Device", "Aerospace", "Military", "Defense", "RF Coaxial", "Industrial Equipment", "Agriculture"], "materials": ["Data cables", "RF coaxial cables", "Smart cables", "Fiber optic cables", "Custom CAT5/6 cable assemblies", "Multi-conductor assemblies", "Specialized overmolding materials"], "equipment": ["CNC machine shop", "30-ton press", "55-ton press", "85-ton press", "Class 1000 clean work area", "Class 10,000 clean work area"], "volume": "High and low volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 30 years of single-focus experience in custom cable and wire harness assemblies", "In-house engineering and design liaison for build-to-print proficiency", "Lean manufacturing practices extended across information and material flows", "Demonstrated overnight ramp-up capability for urgent military needs", "ISO 13485:2016 certified for medical device cable assemblies"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1979 by David Cianciulli -> /about", "Acquired by Amphenol in 2013 -> /", "70,000 sq ft facility in San Jose -> db", "Additional sites in Nogales, Mexico and Malaysia -> /about", "Custom cable harnesses, box builds, overmolded assemblies, discrete assemblies, medical device cables -> /services", "In-house CNC machine shop and presses (30/55/85 ton) -> /", "Class 1000 and Class 10,000 clean work areas -> /", "High and low volume manufacturing -> /", "ISO 13485:2016 certification -> /services", "ITAR registration -> /", "IPC-620:2016 Class III certified parts -> /services", "UL 508 and UL 764 certifications -> /", "C-TPAT, SAM, GDEP certifications -> /", "Industries: Aerospace/Military, Medical Device, Industrial Equipment, Agriculture, RF Coaxial -> /", "Trimble GPS cable ramp-up during Gulf War -> /about", "Lean manufacturing and in-house engineering liaison -> /services", "Single-focus expertise claim -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Amphenol DC Electronics is a custom cable assembly and wire harness manufacturing company.", "founded_year": "1979", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered", "C-TPAT"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='amphenol-dc-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Amphenol TPC Wire & Cable is headquartered in Macedonia, Ohio. The company traces its roots to 1979 when it began supplying ruggedized wire and cable for harsh industrial environments.

The company manufactures high-performance wire, cable, connectors, and assemblies, along with cable management systems, cordsets, and electrical components. A dedicated engineering team of electrical, industrial, and mechanical engineers develops custom-engineered solutions tailored to specific application challenges, from severe abrasion and chemical exposure to extreme temperatures and continuous flexing.

Amphenol TPC serves a broad range of industries including automotive, food and beverage, general manufacturing, industrial automation, metals, mining, oil and gas, rail and transit, shipyard and marine, utility and power transmission, and wood, pulp, and paper. Customers such as a boilermaker leadman at a welding operation, a maintenance manager at a freezer facility, and a prep plant supervisor at a coal mine have reported reduced downtime, lower costs, and improved safety after switching to the company’s Super-Trex® and Chem-Gard® cable lines.

The company differentiates itself by focusing on abuse-resistant designs that outlast commodity cable, emphasizing a problem-solving approach that combines curiosity with qualified engineering expertise.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["High-performance wire manufacturing", "Cable manufacturing", "Connector manufacturing", "Cable assembly manufacturing", "Cable management systems", "Cordset manufacturing", "Electrical component manufacturing", "Custom engineered solutions", "Application engineering support", "Custom cable assembly design", "Custom connector design", "Cable carrier systems", "Storage and deployment systems"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Food and Beverage", "General Manufacturing", "Industrial Automation", "Metals", "Mining", "Oil and Gas", "Rail & Transit", "Ship Yard / Marine", "Utility and Power Transmission", "Wood, Pulp, and Paper"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Engineered to last longer than the average cable", "Abuse-resistant designs for severe service conditions", "Custom-engineered products designed to exact specifications", "In-house team of electrical, industrial, and mechanical engineers", "Proven reduction in downtime, labor, and overall costs"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Macedonia, Ohio -> db", "Founded: 1979 -> /about-us", "Industries served: Automotive, Food and Beverage, General Manufacturing, Industrial Automation, Metals, Mining, Oil and Gas, Rail & Transit, Ship Yard / Marine, Utility and Power Transmission, Wood, Pulp, and Paper -> /about-us", "Products: wire, cable, connectors, assemblies, cable management, cordsets, electrical components, custom solutions -> /about-us", "Testimonials: welding, mining, freezer applications -> /", "Differentiators: engineered to last longer, abuse-resistant, custom-engineered, engineering team -> /about-us", "Company type: manufacturer -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_produ