UPDATE companies SET description='Andersen Manufacturing Inc., doing business as Andersen Hitches, is headquartered in Idaho Falls, Idaho. The company was founded in 1948 and remains family-owned, having grown from a single-room shop into a 102,000-square-foot manufacturing and fabrication complex. In 2021, the facility expanded by an additional 70,000 square feet to meet rising demand.

The company designs and manufactures a full line of trailer hitches and towing accessories, including fifth-wheel connections, bumper-pull hitches, weight-distribution systems, ball mounts, trailer jacks, leveling blocks, and locking pins. Products are built from aluminum, steel, and plastic components, with many items carrying a lifetime warranty.

Its products are sold through a nationwide network of authorized dealers, and the company emphasizes support for local U.S. businesses and jobs.

