UPDATE companies SET description='Andy Sanchez Furniture operates from Algodones, New Mexico, where Andy Sanchez and his sons Aaron and Daniel have been crafting original furniture for nearly three decades. The family-owned workshop, run by Andy and his wife Cheryl alongside their seven children, began with a commitment to creating heirloom pieces that honor the natural character of wood.

The shop specializes in live-edge furniture that incorporates precious stones, gems, and metals into slabs of black walnut, alligator juniper, eucalyptus, and other exotic species. Rather than imposing a design on the material, the artisans let each log’s grain and form dictate the piece, often employing book-matched cuts sourced from dead-standing trees in the Gila National Forest. Every project is a one-off collaboration: clients exchange photos and measurements with the makers to refine dimensions, stone placement, and overall composition until the piece matches the client’s vision.

The clientele consists primarily of residential customers seeking custom tables, chairs, and statement pieces for their homes. Testimonials cite buyers from Pennsylvania and features in New Mexico Magazine, underscoring a reach beyond the local area.

The founders’ guiding principle is to work with nature rather than alter it. As Andy Sanchez puts it, the intention is not to change what has been created but to appreciate what is already provided. This philosophy drives the use of fully cured, dead-standing timber and the practice of pairing wood with stones from the same locale, aiming to produce furniture that gains value and sentiment across generations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Live-edge furniture fabrication", "Stone and gem inlay", "Book matching", "Custom furniture design", "Wood selection and curing", "Client collaboration and iterative design", "Metal integration"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Black walnut", "Alligator juniper", "Eucalyptus", "Exotic woods", "Precious stones", "Gems", "Metals", "Dead-standing wood", "Reclaimed wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Wood-led design process where the material dictates form", "Exclusive use of dead-standing, fully cured timber from Gila National Forest", "Book-matched slabs paired with stones sourced from the same location", "Iterative client collaboration via photo sharing and measurement guidance", "Commitment to heirloom-quality pieces that appreciate in value"], "facts_used": ["Location: Algodones, New Mexico -> db", "Founders: Andy Sanchez, Aaron Sanchez, Daniel Sanchez -> /about-us", "Family-owned -> /about-us", "Nearly 30 years in business -> /about-us", "Live edge furniture with stone and gem inlay -> /", "Wood-led design process -> /about-us", "Book matching technique -> /about-us", "Use of dead-standing wood from Gila National Forest -> /about-us", "Materials: black walnut, alligator juniper, eucalyptus, exotic woods, precious stones, gems, metals -> /, /about-us", "Custom design collaboration with clients -> /", "Testimonials from Deb, Pennsylvania and Dorothy Noe, New Mexico Magazine -> /", "Goal: create heirloom pieces lasting generations -> /about-us", "Philosophy: work with nature, not change it -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Andy Sanchez and his sons are celebrated furniture artists, renowned for their craftsmanship in the creation of remarkable live edge furniture", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='andy-sanchez-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Apex Wire Products Co., Inc. has operated from Franklin Park, Illinois, since 1940. The company specializes in precision wire forming and metal fabrication, serving industrial customers from a facility near Chicago.

The company provides CNC wire forming for diameters from 0.015 to 0.472 inches, using multi-axis equipment to produce complex multi-plane geometries in stainless, low-carbon, spring steels, copper alloys, and specialty grades. In-house capabilities include MIG, TIG, and resistance welding, metal brazing, standard and custom threading, swaging, piercing, and wire straightening and cutting up to 0.750 inches. The shop handles prototype through high-volume runs with traceable documentation at each stage.

Customers span lighting (joist brackets), food and beverage (stainless coffee baskets), education (horizon cradle teaching tools), transportation (bent bolts, U-bolts for automotive and rail), and medical (surgical instruments, implants). The firm also supplies wire components for general industrial assemblies.

Apex emphasizes consolidated in-house production—forming, welding, brazing, threading, and finishing under one roof—to reduce lead times and simplify supply chains. Its in-house tooling and fixture design allows rapid adaptation to special shapes, and every order ships with complete material and process traceability.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC Wire Forming", "MIG Welding", "TIG Welding", "Resistance Welding", "Wire Straightening", "Wire Cutting", "Swaging", "Piercing", "Metal Brazing", "Metal Threading", "Subassembly", "Secondary Finishing", "Quality Inspection", "Tooling & Fixture Design", "Press Brake Forming"], "industries": ["Lighting", "Food & Beverage", "Education", "Transportation", "Medical", "Automotive", "Rail"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Low carbon steel", "Spring steel", "Copper alloys", "Specialty grades", "Aluminum"], "equipment": ["Multi-axis CNC wire forming machines", "Wire straightening and cutting equipment", "Swaging and piercing equipment"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.001 inches on wire straightening and cutting", "built_on": ["In-house tooling and fixture design for rapid adjustments", "Complete traceability and quality documentation on every order", "All forming, welding, brazing, threading, and finishing services under one roof", "Wire straightening and cutting held to \u00b10.001 inch tolerance", "Prototyping to high-volume production on the same equipment"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1940 -> db", "Headquarters Franklin Park, Illinois -> db", "CNC wire forming diameters 0.015\u20130.472 inches -> /", "Multi-axis CNC equipment -> /", "Materials: stainless, low carbon, spring steel, copper alloys, specialty grades -> /", "In-house tooling and fixture design -> /", "MIG, TIG, resistance welding -> /", "Metal brazing -> /", "Metal threading standard and custom -> /", "Wire straightening and cutting diameters 0.015\u20130.750 inches -> /", "Tolera