UPDATE companies SET description='Apocalypse Design Inc. has been designing and manufacturing rugged outdoor gear in Fairbanks, Alaska, since 1983. The company was founded by Dick Flaharty, who named the business after the Apocalypse, a 9,000-foot peak in the remote Revelation Mountains that caught his eye during a winter expedition. Today, the family-owned operation is led by Flaharty''s son Tyson and his wife Davya, both lifelong Alaskans who grew up in Fairbanks and bring extensive endurance-sport experience to the brand.

Every garment and piece of equipment—from expedition parkas and wind anoraks to fleece layers, duffle bags, and backpacks—is designed and sewn at the company''s Fairbanks facility on Minnie Street. The shop focuses on custom manufacturing, meticulous material selection, and innovative pattern work tailored for arctic conditions. All products carry a lifetime warranty against defects in materials and workmanship.

The company''s founding ethos centers on protection, ingenuity, understanding, endurance, and performance—values shaped by the founders'' own adventures on Alaska''s trails and mountains. By keeping design and production under one roof, Apocalypse Design maintains direct control over every stitch, ensuring that each item meets the demands of the environments that inspired its name.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom outdoor gear manufacturing", "Apparel design and sewing", "Material selection and testing", "Pattern development", "Lifetime warranty repair service"], "industries": ["Outdoor adventurers", "Polar explorers", "Climbers", "Dog mushers", "Skiers", "Snow machiners", "Hikers", "Cyclists", "Paddlers", "Scientists", "Film makers", "Pilots", "Sportsmen", "Discerning consumers"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lifetime warranty on all products against defects in materials and workmanship", "Designed and sewn entirely in Fairbanks, Alaska", "Custom manufacturing with innovative, field-tested designs", "Family-owned and operated since 1983"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1983 -> db", "Family-owned and operated -> / (homepage) and /about", "Founder Dick Flaharty -> /about", "Co-owners Tyson and Davya Flaharty -> /about", "Location Fairbanks, Alaska -> / (homepage) and /about", "Products: parkas, anoraks, fleece, wind gear, bags, backpacks -> / (homepage)", "Custom manufacturing and meticulous material selection -> /about", "Lifetime warranty against defects -> /about", "Industries served list -> /about", "Facility address 201 Minnie Street -> / (homepage)", "Named after Apocalypse peak in Revelation Mountains -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Every piece of equipment and clothing is designed and sewn at Apocalypse Design, in Fairbanks, Alaska.", "founded_year": "1983", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order"